on separation (4.5 sigma at 10 GeV/c), outperforming all other candidates both at thinner and thicker configurations, as demonstrated by direct simulation and simulation summary data. No evidence suggests that its performance is compromised over the experiment lifetime given the inert, dry operational environment.\",\"requirements\":[{\"requirement\":\"The radiator must be one of the three candidates listed in candidate_specs.md.\",\"status\":\"met\",\"evidence\":\"Radiator-R1 is listed as a valid candidate in candidate_specs.md.\"},{\"requirement\":\"The radiator must keep its performance over the experiment's lifetime.\",\"status\":\"met\",\"evidence\":\"No mention of degradation for Radiator-R1 exists in specifications or recent documents. Operation is in dry nitrogen, supporting stability.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Radiator thickness between 1 and 6 cm.\",\"status\":\"met\",\"evidence\":\"Selected thickness is 3 cm, which is within range.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Finish by submitting one recommended radiator and thickness.\",\"status\":\"met\",\"evidence\":\"The recommendation is Radiator-R1 at 3 cm based on optimal separation in simulation.\"}]}", "call_id": "call_zcVHyLjxj5UnafQOIwPcb3Jd", "name": "submit_recommendation", "type": "function_call", "id": "fc_0099fc619f48fee7006afcf7fa45f887d0b64ff763d786dab9", "async_": null, "caller": null, "namespace": null, "status": "completed"}]}
